  "releaseNotes": "NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.PostgreSQLOASIS v2.0.3\n\nConnects the OASIS to PostgreSQL — the world's most advanced open-source relational database. Stores OASIS holons and avatars using Npgsql (ADO.NET) with indexed lookup columns and full JSON serialisation. Compatible with PostgreSQL 12+ and managed services (Supabase, Neon, RDS, Azure). Part of the OASIS HOT-Swappable Provider Architecture. Ecosystem: https://oasisomniverse.one\n\nWhat's new since v2.0.2\n- Bind canonical PostgreSQL conformance and fix detail read acknowledgement (1412ca0)\n- Fix PostgreSQL collection counts and prove native storage baseline (5ae53bb)\n- fix(postgres): preserve caller state until acknowledged native writes (f049685)\n- fix(postgres): publish activation state only after native setup succeeds (11ce67a)\n- fix(postgres): reuse unique profile identity selection and verify native duplicates (22870a7)\n- fix(postgres): search canonical persisted text fields with native verification (adefde8)\n- Implement PostgreSQL atomic selected graphs and explicit partial continuation (f01e2dc)\n- Implement PostgreSQL transactional record history with shared codecs and versioned queries (c762dc3)\n- Make PostgreSQL avatar lifecycle atomic and reject stale account revival (61ba7c8)\n- MOVING DOCS AROUND (32a8004)\n- Preserve PostgreSQL holon lifecycle and atomic import outcomes (fc83a57)\n- Restore preserved bounded PostgreSQL CQL implementation with current controls (02252ae)\n- Start breadth-first provider matrix, shared storage conformance and SQL family reuse (c9fb51c)\n\nFull changelog\nhttps://github.com/NextGenSoftwareUK/OASIS/commits/master/Providers/Storage/NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.PostgreSQLOASIS",
